{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea","id":1229401,"title":"Storyteller Plot Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T11:00:56-07:00","id":1229401,"title":"Storyteller Plot Idea","content":"So I've done some Storytelling over the last few years and am building a Mage campaign for some friends. I had an idea for a major plot villain and wanted some feedback on it.<br /> <br /> The Hierophant has been found. Or at least, that's what the Guardians are claiming. They are being secretive about it, and saying he will be arriving in Edmonton shortly. When the day comes, and he does arrive, he is able to demonstrate mastery over 5 different Arcana, specifically Forces, Matter, Spirit, Death, and Mind. In addition to this, his theoretical understanding of Arcana is unrivaled, he seemingly does not have ANY Inferior Aracana (as demonstrated by his ability to related all of the Arcana to each other without the gaps in understanding caused by having an Inferior). <br /> <br /> As icing on the cake, his very presence in the city appears to mitigate Paradox. Mechanically, all mages in the city will receive and additional reach they can use on all spell casting before risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Seems pretty sweet right? Maybe a little too good to be true?<br /> <br /> The twist: An attentive mind might catch that the 5 Arcana that he demonstrates mastery of are infact the 5 Inferior Arcana for the 5 watchtowers. He is not the Hierophant; if anything, he is the Anti-Hierophant. He isn't mitigating Paradox, he's redirecting it. Every time a Mage makes use of the free reach his presence provides, that reach DOES risk paradox, just not at the location the spell is cast. Somewhere in the city, a ball of concentrated Paradox is forming, and each spell cast with the benefits provided makes it a little bit bigger. Once he accumulates enough Paradox, the Anti-Hierophant will unleash it all at once plunging the city/region/country/Fallen World (depending on desired scope of the campaign) into he abyss. If he succeeds, he'll destroy everything. Can the players figure out the problem before it's too late?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:20:53-07:00","id":1229410,"title":"","content":"It's workable, but you're going to want to figure out how they're redirecting Paradox so if the players do figure it out they can come up with plans. You're also going to want to figure out what the Anti-Heirophant is so that players can do research and come up with plans. You don't need to provide solutions to the problems, but there should be hidden information available for players to work with when coming up with their own solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:46:21-07:00","id":1229413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1229410#post1229410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's workable, but you're going to want to figure out how they're redirecting Paradox so if the players do figure it out they can come up with plans. You're also going to want to figure out what the Anti-Heirophant is so that players can do research and come up with plans. You don't need to provide solutions to the problems, but there should be hidden information available for players to work with when coming up with their own solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah definitely on both counts. Need a way for the players to identify what he's doing and roughly how. Maybe no specifics, but they should definitely be able to find clues as to what's happening. Same with his past, being able to get some clues as to who he is, who he was, and maybe some hints of something nefarious. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T15:14:34-07:00","id":1229464,"title":"","content":"I think I\u2019d kick things off after the Anti-Heirophant arrives with a Mage experimenting with just how much the AH being around has increased his power, going way overboard and summoning a Gulmoth. Then you get, an elusive entity that\u2019s probably interested in the Paradox weapon that can sense it as an innate part of its nature, which can drop bread crumbs just by existing. You also probably get an NPC who \u201csummoned an entity to attack the AH\u201d going on trial at the Consilium and/or under threat of assassination from the Guardians. If the Mage that\u2019s summoned the Gulmoth is tied to the players by close alliance then it can sow the seeds for not trusting the AH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T18:09:34-07:00","id":1229490,"title":"","content":"Also, come to think of it there have been false Heirophants before which is why there would also be a Guardian faction trying to assassinate the AH (All thrones are false). Another source for potential conflict or information, allies in unlikely places or people with similar goals getting in the way as they try to remain clandestine and feel their secrecy is threatened by the PCs investigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T13:49:08-07:00","id":1229855,"title":"","content":"Isn't the belief in the Heiromagus a secret the Guardians keep from all but their most trustworthy members ? Even when there is a potential candidate, they would actively try to sabotage him, because if he is the real deal, then he will have the Wisdom to overcome trials most mages wouldn't. So one option is that the Guardians use some leverage on the party to make them investigate him, observe him, test him and so on. The basic idea is that they would use blackmail to make sure the player cabal remains discrete. The they hand out missions and give nice perks for completion, like imbued items, a safehouse, a few favors, things to sweeten the deal. So why doesn't the Order handle it themselves ? Because an influential masters feels there is already enough evidence to support his claim and wants to set him on the road to success (this master is a Scelestus). However other, more sceptic masters do not agree and are ultimately who setup the party's missions (behind layers of indirection, as the Guardians like to do).<br /> <br /> You can also throw in an outsider to plant seeds of suspicion. For example, an Aegis Kai Doru who is conducting a parallel investigation and is willing to help the party, or throw in a surprisingly sane Banisher who only targets the AH (he Awoke when his town and by extension his mage wife were consumed by the AH testing his plan on a smaller scale ) or even the old &quot;crackpot&quot; Nameless mage that keeps warning people, fearful that his visions come to pass. You can even have the Seers begin attacking in an almost suicidal manner, because either they wipe out this threat ASAP or the Exarchs will send an ochemata down to take care of it, Unmaking everything nearby (flesh, minds, souls, spirits, everything) as a &quot;safety zone when removing this cancer&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can also have the Paradox buildup cause a massive stir in the Shadow, with the original inhabitants of the area fleeing in a panic, even high ranked spirits resorting to possession, others searching for asylum or even new haunts. All that can point them in the right direction.<br /> <br /> I think it would be cool if they earned the info of what the Hieromagus even is and in the process see how such a person appearing rattles even the shadowy Guardians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-24-2018, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T14:34:45-07:00","id":1229863,"title":"","content":"Just want to throw a quick term correction I was just reminded of, Heirophant is an official position, the Guardians are waiting for the Heiromagus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T03:06:50-07:00","id":1229961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1229855#post1229855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the belief in the Heiromagus a secret the Guardians keep from all but their most trustworthy members ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an esoteric tenet, so you just need to be a fully initiated Guardian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T08:59:47-07:00","id":1230024,"title":"","content":"I believe it came up before on the forums of just how secret it is, my memory is very hazy on this topic, but I'm pretty sure that other Mages are aware that the Guardians are waiting for a messianic figure but don't have any details beyond that. If you think about it, the smart move on the Guardians part would be to spill the beans on their beliefs, but only the most safe/boring parts so that other Mages don't get Obsessed and dig into their stuff. Which, I guess is what the Exoteric Beliefs are about anyway, but it would make sense to have exoteric cover stories for all their esoteric stuff as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:19:35-07:00","id":1230027,"title":"","content":"An interesting idea.<br /> <br /> As others have pointed out, the whole hieromagus idea isn't really widespread outside the Guardians, but I can see a group of them going public with it if they think the messiah is here.<br /> As fun as the most oblivious use of said group is, as deadly magic-ninja bodyguards, if I recall correctly, part of the hieromagus\u2019s \u201cduties\u201d was passing judgment on the Guardians for their sins. Maybe there are some who don't like the whole judged bit and try to discredit the false Messiah. Pontential allies for the PC-s abound.<br /> <br /> Other than that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea#post1229401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once he accumulates enough Paradox, the Anti-Hierophant will unleash it all at once plunging the city/region/country/Fallen World (depending on desired scope of the campaign) into he abyss. If he succeeds, he'll destroy everything. Can the players figure out the problem before it's too late?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s just my opinion, and you can do whatever you want on your table, bit I have a personal bias against the whole mass-destruction for whatever petty reason. Of course there may be a reason that makes sense, and the character may as well be insane(and seeing that He is dicking around with the Abyss he probably is.) but its probably not the way I would spin it.<br /> <br /> As I try to keep my antagonists both sympathetic and understandable, here is something:<br /> <br /> The collected paradox isn\u2019t just a bomb(at least the A-H thinks it isn\u2019t). It is part of a summoning ritual, bringing one of the Annunaki the stillborn universes and cast of timelines that live in the abyss. Should the PC-s fail the Anunnaki\u2019s alternate history will overwrite the fallen world. The A-H thinks that said history is objectively better that the current one and tries to use it to bring a new golden age for humanity. (Perhaps he\u2019s even right.)<br /> <br /> In the event of failure the PC-s somehow survive unchanged(Perhaps inside an archmage\u2019 golden road or an emnation realm) and are stranded in the new world.<br /> They must gather those who similarly unchanged, and restore the world to its proper state.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, if you go with a golden road as the way of survival, most of the survivors will probably be seers, as they actively include archmages in their hierarchies and thus the most likely to be in a golden road when the paradox hits. But then you are involving archmages, so an alternative may be better.<br /> <br /> As they investigate the new timeline (whatever you decide it may be) they discover that their timeline got displaced into the abyss and now lives ass one of the Annunaki.<br /> They must replicate the A-H\u2019s ritual to bring it back.(That it may be the original time-line and theirs is the invader probably best implied but not confirmed.)<br /> <br /> Granted it only really works in a global plot, but probably can be scaled back(Not an annunaki but an abyssal watchtower that gets Summoned for example.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T10:23:00-07:00","id":1230041,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty cool, and since the Invader timeline is an Abyssal manifestation, I guess magic will work differently. I wonder how much more difficult it would be to keep Wisdom in a world where Paradox is common and Supernal mages are seen as the Scelestus (because everyone Awakens to a Dur-Abzu).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T11:30:55-07:00","id":1230059,"title":"","content":"Some extra to my previous post regarding the seers.<br /> <br /> As the Hieromagus will supposedly overthrow the Exarchs, they probably will send a few assassins on principle, even if they don\u2019t believe it to be the real thing. (thought it can be potentially taken as a confirmation, so they may try to debunk him first.) And if they get wind of the whole Scelesti thing, it is written in the job description: \u201cRegulate the Abyss.\u201d An Abyssal incursion on that scale could get the whole tethrarchy mobilized, with possible ochemata support.<br /> <br /> It is a possible source of the golden road, if you go with my alternate timeline idea. The PC are part of a (possibly suicidal) assault on a Tethrarch\u2019s Chantry and as they face the arch-master, the summoning goes of.<br /> <br /> It could be even played from the side of the seers: Heroically trying to prevent the crazed Scelestus from ending the world as we know it. While trying to not end the world in an all out war with the misguided mages that stand between you and Him. And if you are at it, why nor recruit some of said misguided mages to the glory of the Exarchs and your personal prestige.(Its my headcanon that the Pentacle loses more members to the recruiters of the seers than direct violence between the two groups.)<br /> <br /> It\u2019s even a possible hook for nameless characters (PC or NPC). As tension rises between the rival sects: they try to diffuse it by removing the point of conflict. Either by debunking the Hieromagus (even falsifying evidence to debunk him) or try to kill him in such way, that it doesn\u2019t trigger a war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1230041#post1230041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds pretty cool, and since the Invader timeline is an Abyssal manifestation, I guess magic will work differently. I wonder how much more difficult it would be to keep Wisdom in a world where Paradox is common and Supernal mages are seen as the Scelestus (because everyone Awakens to a Dur-Abzu).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is possible( maybe even probable), but I would not make it an unlivable hellscape. I metionaed the possibility of the Hieromagus being correct about it being better, and that is probably what I would go with.<br /> As specific inspiration: in the TaMNI:New testament Light novell the (at the time) big bad ,in order to break the protagonist\u2019s resolve, brings him to a world where everyone he has ever lived lives a happier life, and the major tragedies of their lives never happened. Except that in that timeline the protagonist never existed at all.<br /> I wouldn\u2019t go that far but make it in some visible way better than the original. Possibly with some flaws at deeper investigation, but better enough to make the characters question if bringing back the original timeline is the correct choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T09:52:58-07:00","id":1231133,"title":"","content":"Some fantastic ideas, and yeah sorry for not verifying the term, Hieromagus is the correct word. I've just been reading Practical Guide to Evil a lot and Hierophant is one of the characters. (I highly recommend that online book for WOD and Exalted fans as the Named in it remind me of Exalted levels of power)<br /> <br /> I love the idea of going the Annunaki route as I was a big fan of the Prince of a Thousand Leaves in the Boston book and used it in my first attempt at a Mage Chronicle. <br /> <br /> I should mention that the Seers were recently kicked out of the city due to the Hierach activating an Artifact his Cabal dug up. Part of the campaign would be focused around realizing he did that by way of human sacrifice and drawing on the Abyss. He really does have everyones best interests at heart, and is willing to sacrifice his soul for what he believes in. The first part of the campaign was going to be focused on cleaning up all the messes left when all the Seers were suddenly and very abruptly evicted from the city, leaving their various experiments and Sanctums unattended. I even have a short story I wrote about one of the Seers in the city, taking place just before the eviction. Partly as a writing exercise for myself, and partly to help me flesh out his character. I planned on having him taking advantage of the situation to undermine his competitors among the Seers and elevate himself higher int he Tetrachy (spelling?). Seeing as he can't get into the city himself, using the players as pawns to weaken his opponents would be his approach, offering them tidbits of minor artifacts and worthless arcane lore for their help. In addition, he'd help them hunt down and capture the Selestus that's infiltrated their ranks (after all, the Abyss is as bad for the Seers as it is for the Pentacle).<br /> <br /> I also am going to have at least one Selestus hiding among the Pentacle mages. <br /> <br /> As for this New World which could end up replacing the Fallen World should the players fail to stop the AH, I love the idea of it being actually better. Like, objectively better. But I'd lean towards having it that their own loved ones are not around. Maybe vastly reduced presence of things that go bump in the night? An abundance of positive spirits of things like Love, Joy, Laughter, etc. I know all spirits can be a problem in the wrong situation, but maybe not in this New World. Hell, maybe even have it that Sleepers don't increase the risk of Paradox and Mages can practice out in the open. But again, none of the people they know and love are here. The AH was right, this world is better, but it isn't THEIR world.<br /> <br /> As to getting them into that world intact and unchanged, yeah there's a number of ways that could be accomplished. Maybe a Golden Road, or a pocket dimension, or even being close to the AH when it goes off (after all he'd want to keep his knowledge of what he'd done and why so maybe he has a field setup to isolate himself).<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who's posted so far, I'm getting a lot of wonderful inspiration from reading these replies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:59:16-07:00","id":1231152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1231133#post1231133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some fantastic ideas, and yeah sorry for not verifying the term, Hieromagus is the correct word. I've just been reading Practical Guide to Evil a lot and Hierophant is one of the characters. (I highly recommend that online book for WOD and Exalted fans as the Named in it remind me of Exalted levels of power)</div> </div> </div> </div> I wholeheartedly second this recommendation. The Guide is Awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1231133#post1231133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I love the idea of going the Annunaki route as I was a big fan of the Prince of a Thousand Leaves in the Boston book and used it in my first attempt at a Mage Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Glad to help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1231133#post1231133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I should mention that the Seers were recently kicked out of the city due to the Hierach activating an Artifact his Cabal dug up. Part of the campaign would be focused around realizing he did that by way of human sacrifice and drawing on the Abyss. He really does have everyones best interests at heart, and is willing to sacrifice his soul for what he believes in. The first part of the campaign was going to be focused on cleaning up all the messes left when all the Seers were suddenly and very abruptly evicted from the city, leaving their various experiments and Sanctums unattended. I even have a short story I wrote about one of the Seers in the city, taking place just before the eviction. Partly as a writing exercise for myself, and partly to help me flesh out his character. I planned on having him taking advantage of the situation to undermine his competitors among the Seers and elevate himself higher int he Tetrachy (spelling?). Seeing as he can't get into the city himself, using the players as pawns to weaken his opponents would be his approach, offering them tidbits of minor artifacts and worthless arcane lore for their help. In addition, he'd help them hunt down and capture the Selestus that's infiltrated their ranks (after all, the Abyss is as bad for the Seers as it is for the Pentacle).</div> </div> </div> </div> There's quite a bit of potential here.<br /> Please note that the potential fallout of evicting the Seers isn't limited to the experiments and sanctums.<br /> The Seers have a nasty habit of integrating themselves into mortal power structures. If someone high enough in the ladder vanishes it will both seriously disrupt the operation of the given organization, and launch a mundane investigation. And depending how the Evicting spell worked, there may be mundane minions in the city remaining.<br /> The other possible fallout is the Bound. There may or may not be an old god sealed under the city,but even the threat of there being one can be a serious bargaining chip.<br /> If there's then either its malicious, and wouldn't they want to consult the professionals on keeping it sealed, or it isn't in which case it can be a serious resource, even thought it must be supplied with not inconsiderable amount of mana.<br /> <br /> The Seers book describes the iron piramid's working as the Pylons from below the Tehrarchy from above. Now that they lost the people on the ground they may lean on the latter more.<br /> Economic manipulation, perhaps even manipulating the Astral to influence the people, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Furthermore if the AH's plan gets out, the either facing the destruction of a city(on low end) or the End of The World as We Know It (on the high end). They aren't gonna pull any punches.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T11:26:39-07:00","id":1231165,"title":"","content":"I'd have at least one thing (other than them and their dearest not being there) as wrong still in the &quot;better world&quot;. That way the PCs can use it as their line-in-the-sand (however much it might be exaggerated for justification). Like, there is world peace, but no ice cream, or a lack of poverty, but no [insert pet of choice]. That way it isn't telling them &quot;the world is better off without you and yours&quot;/&quot;you are what is wrong with the world&quot;. They can at least say &quot;A world without pie isn't really a world worth living in anyways&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T08:27:19-07:00","id":1232134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1231165#post1231165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have at least one thing (other than them and their dearest not being there) as wrong still in the &quot;better world&quot;. That way the PCs can use it as their line-in-the-sand (however much it might be exaggerated for justification). Like, there is world peace, but no ice cream, or a lack of poverty, but no [insert pet of choice]. That way it isn't telling them &quot;the world is better off without you and yours&quot;/&quot;you are what is wrong with the world&quot;. They can at least say &quot;A world without pie isn't really a world worth living in anyways&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> My thought on that was a little more diabolical, because upon thinking more on it I came to this same conclusion. The entire world is united in one religion, so no religious bigotry or violence. Problem being the religion they are united under is an unpleasant one. Haven't decided on any yet but considering something ancient from South America (and the associated blood sacrifices to grease the wheels of creation) or even have it a straight up Abyssal entity being worshiped. Another option I thought of was that all the mages of this new world are Seers. Every single one of them. These sorts of things the players would have to figure out, and that likely wouldn't happen if the players just decide to reverse what the AH did. If they just decide to undo it, they may not realize just how bad things actually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T11:57:24-07:00","id":1232195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsarnok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1229401-storyteller-plot-idea?p=1231152#post1231152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's quite a bit of potential here.<br /> Please note that the potential fallout of evicting the Seers isn't limited to the experiments and sanctums.<br /> The Seers have a nasty habit of integrating themselves into mortal power structures. If someone high enough in the ladder vanishes it will both seriously disrupt the operation of the given organization, and launch a mundane investigation. And depending how the Evicting spell worked, there may be mundane minions in the city remaining.<br /> The other possible fallout is the Bound. There may or may not be an old god sealed under the city,but even the threat of there being one can be a serious bargaining chip.<br /> If there's then either its malicious, and wouldn't they want to consult the professionals on keeping it sealed, or it isn't in which case it can be a serious resource, even thought it must be supplied with not inconsiderable amount of mana.<br /> <br /> The Seers book describes the iron piramid's working as the Pylons from below the Tehrarchy from above. Now that they lost the people on the ground they may lean on the latter more.<br /> Economic manipulation, perhaps even manipulating the Astral to influence the people, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Furthermore if the AH's plan gets out, the either facing the destruction of a city(on low end) or the End of The World as We Know It (on the high end). They aren't gonna pull any punches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about the possibility of Bound I'll admit. Though the cities population of mages is rather low, (small city and I like having a comprehensive caste list) so I can easily have it that there are not any there. On the other hand... potential for DOOM! Having them going to the Seers to ask advice on how to keep it's prison intact and solid could be rather amusing. Especially when the Guardians come knocking asking what they were doing talking to the enemy.<br /> <br /> The Seers themselves can't set foot in the city, but they are still using intermediaries, sleepwalkers, and Profane Urims as well as sympathetic magic. A couple of them are going to be more negatively affected than others due to the nature of their work (one is a psychiatrist who's practice will be put on hold due to an 'unforeseen and immediate medical emergency'). In addition, the effect isn't going to be perfect, every now and then one of them finds a way in. Though once the Hierarch hears about it, he can plug the hole so they can't use the same method again. This last bit is for me to be able to have the Seers able to come in when I want them to, and not when I don't. <br /> <br /> The players will be contacted by the Augur of one of the Pylons. His Pylon is made up of an alliance of Panopticon, Paternoster, and Preatorians. They are working together against the more established Pylon of the Hegemony. Again, small population, they don't like each other, but it's the best way to bring down the servants of Unity. <br /> <br /> And yes, if they find out about AH's plan, they'll drop everything to stop him. Seeing as he's in the city, that will likely mean trying to help the players stop him as best they can. Even before they figure out his plan, they'll be keeping an eye on him and doing what they can to turn the cities Wise against him (digging up dirt from his past etc). <br /> <br /> Keep it coming, this is really helping me flesh out my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T20:17:38-07:00","id":1232786,"title":"","content":"Building on what you said, how about putting pressure to make the decision ? In this world they have a huge world tree (think like the one in the Tales series), however, they need to feed it a sacrifice every once in a while, depending on an augury. Specific werewolves, vampires, mages, mortals, demons, etc. So long as the tree stands strong, nature provides everything and new, clean, eco friendly technology was created, which can organically interface with the user, allowing great precision. For how weapons and the Seers would look in this world, look at the Yuuzhan Vong. So even if the world continues not being perfect, there is less violence, less hunger, less disease and people are overall healthier.<br /> <br /> The downside is that the people consumed become fruit for the tree, each one bearing the face of the person whose whole (mind, body, soul, mana, etc) are contained within. And they form a pattern, you see, they each are positioned in the pressure points of a human body. When all are complete, they will become a vessel for it, sealing the omens of the world tree and it will ascend. Yes, an Abyssal entity became an archmage and can ascend....don't look at me, I gave up on making any logical sense out of the Abyss long ago, logic is part of Supernal Truth, after all.<br /> <br /> So what now ? The world is not perfect, but much better. The world tree seems benign, but what happens if it ascends ? What happens to the world that depends on it ? It will have the power to set things right, but what does having an Abyssal symbol as a Truth do to the fundamentals of magic ? What will happen to Paradox ?<br /> <br /> The way to make everything go back to normal is to have it be consumed by the Abyss. This could lead to the Pax Arcana being in a frenzy and maybe even make the Order of The Gate be your biggest allies in this quest. Best of all, if they are not discrete, the party could be seen as Banishers or Scelestus by others, actually bringing the Pentacle and Seers to ally in preventing the world tree from being destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-05-2018, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}